WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.709
Measure from the usage fields, not from the text.

2
00:00:02.989 --> 00:00:09.133
Every Claude response carries a usage object, and it is the only ground truth for what a request cost.

3
00:00:09.413 --> 00:00:14.661
Four meters matter for pricing: input_tokens: input processed at the full price.

4
00:00:14.941 --> 00:00:19.720
With caching on, this is only the uncached remainder after the last cache breakpoint.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.845
cache_creation_input_tokens: input written to the cache this request, billed at a premium (1.

6
00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:31.032
25 times base input for the five-minute lifetime, 2 times for one hour).

7
00:00:31.312 --> 00:00:33.936
The cache_creation object splits it by lifetime.

8
00:00:34.216 --> 00:00:40.637
cache_read_input_tokens: input served from the cache, billed at a small fraction of base input (0.

9
00:00:40.917 --> 00:00:42.944
05 times on Opus 5.

10
00:00:43.224 --> 00:00:44.717
5 and Sonnet 5.

11
00:00:44.997 --> 00:00:46.107
5, 0.

12
00:00:46.387 --> 00:00:49.523
1 times on most other models, at the time of writing).

13
00:00:49.803 --> 00:00:53.771
output_tokens: everything the model generated, thinking included.

14
00:00:54.051 --> 00:01:00.771
The prompt-caching docs give the identity to remember: total input equals the three input meters added together.

15
00:01:01.051 --> 00:01:06.768
If a dashboard charts input_tokens alone, a well-cached agent looks like it sends almost nothing.

16
00:01:07.048 --> 00:01:09.139
Three habits make the numbers trustworthy.

17
00:01:09.419 --> 00:01:14.880
Log every response’s usage with a task id, so you can roll requests up into tasks.

18
00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:20.429
Price from a table with a “checked on” date, kept in configuration, because prices change.

19
00:01:20.709 --> 00:01:38.501
Reconcile monthly against the provider’s own numbers: Anthropic’s Usage and Cost API (which needs an Admin API key) reports usage by model, workspace, API key, and service tier, and costs in USD, typically within about five minutes of a request completing.

20
00:01:38.781 --> 00:01:47.400
If your computed total and the provider’s total disagree by more than rounding, something in your logging is wrong, and you want to know before finance does.

21
00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:51.051
Other providers expose the same idea with different names.

22
00:01:51.331 --> 00:01:54.104
OpenAI reports cached input as usage.

23
00:01:54.384 --> 00:01:55.835
input_tokens_details.

24
00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:57.843
cached_tokens, for example.

25
00:01:58.123 --> 00:02:02.880
When you compare providers, normalize every response into one record shape first.
